  {
    "id": "ex-c20b77vk",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "cancellation",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Inside `finally` in a cancelled coroutine, you call a `suspend` function to save the session. What happens, and what fixes it?",
    "hint": "The coroutine is already cancelled.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "It works: `finally` is exempt from cancellation",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "`finally` runs, but suspending calls in it throw."
      },
      {
        "text": "It throws; `withContext(NonCancellable)` lets it run",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "It hangs until the program ends",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It throws at once."
      },
      {
        "text": "It runs on another thread automatically",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Nothing moves it."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-g765ezpc",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "failure",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Inside `coroutineScope`, one `launch` throws. What happens to the other children?",
    "hint": "`reminder sync cancelled`, `export cancelled`.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "They finish their work normally",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Neither printed its result."
      },
      {
        "text": "They are cancelled",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right, and their `finally` blocks run."
      },
      {
        "text": "They are restarted",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Nothing restarts."
      },
      {
        "text": "They keep running after the scope has already returned to its caller",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A scope never returns before its children finish."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-mqe8e20f",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "failure",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "After cancelling the siblings, what does `coroutineScope` do with the failure?",
    "hint": "`refresh failed: calendar unreachable`.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "Logs it and returns normally",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "`main` had to catch it."
      },
      {
        "text": "Swallows it",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "`main` received it."
      },
      {
        "text": "Rethrows it to its caller",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "Retries the failed child once before giving up and returning",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "There is no retry."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-hdtgfgej",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "supervisor",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Which work suits `supervisorScope` rather than `coroutineScope`?",
    "hint": "Separate jobs, or parts of one result?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "Loading the week and the goal to draw one screen",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Without either there is no screen: one result."
      },
      {
        "text": "Sending a reminder to each of three devices",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: independent jobs."
      },
      {
        "text": "Two `async` loads whose results are combined",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Parts of one result."
      },
      {
        "text": "Any work at all on Android",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "The choice depends on the work, not the platform."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-v1dfb1ja",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "supervisor",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "In `supervisorScope`, what is the `CoroutineExceptionHandler` for?",
    "hint": "The scope does not propagate the failure.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "To retry the failed child",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It only reports."
      },
      {
        "text": "To cancel the siblings after a failure",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That is what a supervisor avoids."
      },
      {
        "text": "To make the scope throw to its caller",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "A supervisor scope does not."
      },
      {
        "text": "To handle a failure nobody else caught",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: a last resort."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-yzka34kn",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "timeouts",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "`withTimeoutOrNull(500) { slowServer(2000) }`. What does it return?",
    "hint": "The server takes four times the limit.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`null`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "The week, after 2000 ms",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It gave up at 500."
      },
      {
        "text": "It throws `TimeoutCancellationException`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That is `withTimeout`."
      },
      {
        "text": "An empty list, which the server returns when it is too slow",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Nothing invents a list."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-vyst17c4",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "timeouts",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Without its last `println`, `Timeout.kt`'s `main` broke the whole project. Why?",
    "hint": "What type was `main`?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`withTimeout` cannot be used in `main`",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It is used there in the final version."
      },
      {
        "text": "A `main` not returning `Unit` collides with the other `main`s",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right: conflicting overloads."
      },
      {
        "text": "`try` without `finally` is not allowed as the last expression of a function",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It is allowed; its type was the issue."
      },
      {
        "text": "Gradle runs only the first `main` it finds",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "`-Pmain` picks one."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-v68j8stq",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "pitfalls",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "Why did `tick 1` to `tick 4` print after the job was cancelled?",
    "hint": "What did `runCatching` catch?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "`cancelAndJoin` waits for the loop to end before cancelling",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It cancelled at 150 ms."
      },
      {
        "text": "`runCatching` swallowed each `CancellationException`",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right."
      },
      {
        "text": "`repeat` cannot be cancelled",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It is an ordinary loop; the catch was the problem."
      },
      {
        "text": "The ticks were buffered",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "They ran after cancellation."
      }
    ]
